WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.900
NOW, BEFORE I ANNOUNCE THE
NOMINEES FOR BEST LIVE ACTION

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.560
SHORT, I'VE GOT A QUESTION FOR
ALL THE NOMINEES HERE.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.070
CAN I GET A QUICK SHOW OF HANDS?

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:11.040
HOW MANY OF YOU STARTED OFF YOUR
CAREER WORKING AS CAST OR CREW

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.840
ON A SHORT FILM?

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.730
I'M NOTICING SOME OF THE PEOPLE
GO STRAIGHT TO THE TOP.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.730
EXACTLY.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.869
LOOK, YOU CAN ALWAYS BE SURE THE
CATEGORY FOR BEST LIVE ACTION

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:24.019
SHORT WILL SHOWCASE SOME OF
TOMORROW'S GREAT FILMMAKERS.

00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:25.989
AND YOU CAN UNDERSTAND WHY.

00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:27.710
BUILDING A WORLD, DRAWING AN

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.579
AUDIENCE INTO IT, TAKING THEM
ON AN UNFORGETTABLE RIDE

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:32.860
OVER AN HOUR OR TWO IS
DIFFICULT ENOUGH

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.400
TO DO IT IN UNDER 20 MINUTES
IS A MIRACLE.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.060
IF FEATURE FILMS ARE NOVELS,
SHORT FILMS ARE LIKE POEMS.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.230
THEY HAVE LESS SPACE TO WORK
WITH, BUT THE DISTILLED VISION

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:44.130
THEY CONTAIN, CAN OFTEN
MAKE EVEN MORE OF AN IMPACT.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:47.790
HERE ARE THE NOMINEES FOR BEST
LIVE ACTION SHORT FILM.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:53.390
“FEELING THROUGH,” DOUG ROLAND
AND SUSAN RUZENSKI.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:58.355
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:00:58.355 --> 00:01:02.370
“THE LETTER ROOM,” ELVIRA LIND
AND SOFIA SONDERVAN.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.919
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:01:06.919 --> 00:01:11.759
“THE PRESENT,” FARAH NABULSI AND
OSSAMA BAWARDI.

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:14.615
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:01:14.615 --> 00:01:19.700
“TWO DISTANT STRANGERS,” TRAVON
FREE AND MARTIN DESMOND ROE.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.264
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:01:23.264 --> 00:01:29.384
“WHITE EYE,” TOMER SHUSHAN AND
SHIRA HOCHMAN.

00:01:29.384 --> 00:01:32.851
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:01:32.851 --> 00:01:34.920
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:40.825
“TWO DISTANT STRANGERS, TRAVON
FREE AND MARTIN DESMOND ROE.

00:01:40.825 --> 00:01:46.185
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.327
OH, MY GOD.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.292
OH, GOD IS SO GOOD.

00:02:09.082 --> 00:02:14.660
TODAY, THE POLICE WILL KILL
THREE PEOPLE.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.690
AND TOMORROW, THE POLICE WILL
KILL THREE PEOPLE.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.950
AND THE DAY AFTER THAT, THE
POLICE WILL KILL THREE PEOPLE.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:25.520
BECAUSE ON AVERAGE, THE POLICE
IN AMERICA EVERY DAY KILL THREE PEOPLE.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.620
WHICH AMOUNTS TO ABOUT
1,000 PEOPLE A YEAR.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.560
AND THOSE PEOPLE HAPPEN TO
DISPROPORTIONATELY

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.570
BE BLACK PEOPLE.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.210
AND, YOU KNOW,
JAMES BALDWIN ONCE SAID

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.610
THE MOST DESPICABLE THING
A PERSON CAN BE IS INDIFFERENT

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.140
TO OTHER PEOPLE'S PAIN.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:46.290
AND SO I JUST ASK THAT
YOU PLEASE NOT BE INDIFFERENT.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:52.360
PLEASE DON'T BE INDIFFERENT
TO OUR PAIN.

